    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HHD2C7E83A687FC6145C3ED8F7D22FC54D" xlink:to="HH37E3D4FDF2D8EE4446B872B0CD035A25" order="1" />
    <link:loc xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="#HH698772B00AE9A8F1B89607A6BBF9DF81" xlink:label="HH698772B00AE9A8F1B89607A6BBF9DF81" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HHDA6714F1F4AEFC8CD05D0BE61096E467" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Page 324 Line 15 Col B Pursuant to FERC Order 668, for FERC purposes MGE nets RTO day-ahead and real-time energy market activity separately on an hourly basis. For PSCW and SEC reporting, the RTO hourly day-ahead and real-time activity is combined for netting purposes. Due to the netting difference, Purchased Power expenses are $6,050,124.00 greater for FERC purposes than PSCW or SEC purposes for the six months ended June 30, 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HH698772B00AE9A8F1B89607A6BBF9DF81" xlink:to="HHDA6714F1F4AEFC8CD05D0BE61096E467" order="1" />
